  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Eastern Air Express has $224M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Eastern Air Express received 61 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.7M, and obligations are up 3870.1% year over year. Eastern Air Express shows a rapid increase from prior years: obligations were $5.6M in FY25, $2.2M in FY24, $2.9M in FY23, $3.3K in FY22, and $0 in FY21. Eastern Air Express’s FY2026 obligations are concentrated with a few agencies: the Department of Homeland Security obligated $216M, the Department of Defense obligated $5.6M, and the Department of the Interior obligated $3M. Eastern Air Express’s current-year totals are partial, representing fiscal year to date contract obligations. Eastern Air Express’s award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations. Eastern Air Express’s data reflects obligations only for the current fiscal year to date and prior full fiscal years as listed.",
